{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AptabaseEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"AptabaseEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"AptabaseEncoding","role":"collection"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for Aptabase in one call. It checks your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key and takes the region from it: an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-EU-"},{"type":"text","text":" key posts to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/eu.aptabase.com\/api\/v0\/events"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-US-"},{"type":"text","text":" key to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/us.aptabase.com\/api\/v0\/events"},{"type":"text","text":", and a self-hosted "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-SH-"},{"type":"text","text":" key to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/api\/v0\/events"},{"type":"text","text":" under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"host"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass. The key goes in each request’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"App-Key"},{"type":"text","text":" header field,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes the body. Each batch is split to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": 25 events a request, the most Aptabase takes, and 1,000,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes a request, the encoder’s own bound, under the 1 MiB that nginx takes by default in front of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many self-hosted servers. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and also 418, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase answers when a request’s body arrives slower than 60 bytes a second after a 10-second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grace period, as over a poor connection ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). It drops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out, so import"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What Aptabase does with these events depends on more than the events themselves:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase counts users itself. Its server hashes each request’s IP address and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User-Agent"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header field with a salt it changes every day, so a user is one network address and client on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one day. The destination sends no user or device identifier; it can’t keep the server from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seeing the address a request comes from.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase looks up each request’s IP address and stores its country and region with every event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the request, so its dashboard breaks counts down by where the requests came from."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Its sessions are the sessions enricher’s. A record with no session, from a tracker without the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enricher, counts as a session of one event. A record a store recovered after a relaunch keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its session.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its breakdowns by operating system, app version, build, device model and locale come from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context. Give the tracker the standard context enrichers, or those breakdowns are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty. A recovered record keeps only the session of its context, so it shows none of them."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"type":"text","text":" decides where events go. Aptabase shows events marked as debug events only in its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Debug mode, apart from your users’ events, and keeps them for months rather than years."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase requires an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sdkVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" with every event, and keeps it, but its events dashboard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t show it. The destination always sends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The app key is public, as Aptabase’s own SDKs ship it inside every app, and the events API takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no other credential, so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to Aptabase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import AptabaseEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let aptabase = try HTTPDestination.aptabase(","    appKey: appKey,  \/\/ from the app's Instructions page: A-EU-…, A-US-… or A-SH-…","    isDebug: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose events only Debug mode should show","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions(), .application(), .device(), .operatingSystem(), .locale()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: aptabase)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a self-hosted server, pass the URL it is reached at as "},{"code":"host","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"https:\/\/aptabase.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with a path where it is served under one; the destination appends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\/api\/v0\/events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A host must be "},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseSetupError","type":"reference"},{"text":": for a key that is empty or only whitespace; for one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-"},{"text":", a region, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":" and a body of ASCII letters and digits; for a region other than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EU"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"US"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SH"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEV"},{"text":", in capitals; for a self-hosted key without a host, or a cloud key with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one; and for a host that isn’t a plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"text":" URL, or that already ends in the endpoint. A key of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a server run in development (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-DEV-"},{"text":") is taken as a self-hosted one, so it needs the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"development server’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"text":" URL as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"host"},{"text":": Aptabase’s SDKs default to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/localhost:3000"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for such a key, which the factory refuses, so serve the development server over TLS. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"text":" has no default:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" for builds whose events only Debug mode should show, such as debug builds.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Sessions","anchor":"Sessions","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher: its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a lowercase UUID. Nothing else identifies a record: no vendor identifier, device identifier or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account, and no trace context. A record with no session has its own identifier as its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","text":": making up a session would join unrelated records, skipping the record would lose it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and Aptabase takes no event without a session."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What Aptabase receives","anchor":"What-Aptabase-receives","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a JSON array of events. Every event has:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"eventName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the event’s name;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","text":", the session;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so an event sent late still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counts at the time it was tracked;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"systemProps"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osName"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appBuildNumber"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceModel"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"},{"type":"text","text":", the locale’s language and region ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"},{"type":"text","text":"), each when the record’s context has it;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"type":"text","text":", as you pass it; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sdkVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":". A context value longer than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase takes (30 characters of the system’s name, 100 of its version, 50 of the app’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"version, 20 of its build and 100 of the device’s model) is left out and the event is sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without it, as Aptabase would refuse the whole request. A long build number such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2026.11.27.1432-abc1234"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out of every event the build sends, so its breakdown is empty."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The encoder logs a notice the first time it leaves out each one;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"props"},{"text":", when the event has any to send.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made with. Aptabase keeps strings, numbers and booleans, and only a placeholder for an object or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an array, so an object or array is flattened into dotted names: a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart"},{"text":" holding ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"text":", and the first element of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"text":". A boolean stays a boolean, which Aptabase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":"; a number keeps its JSON type; and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" property is left out. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase stores a number as a .NET "},{"code":"decimal","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it keeps 28 decimal places and rounds a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fraction away."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name is only whitespace or longer than the 60 characters Aptabase takes, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Aptabase refuses the whole request holding one;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a property, once flattened, whose name is empty, only whitespace or longer than 40","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters, which Aptabase would drop;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a string value longer than 180 characters, which Aptabase would cut short;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a number of magnitude 2⁹⁶ (about 7.9 × 10²⁸) or more, past a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"decimal"},{"text":", for which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Aptabase fails the whole request;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one tracked more than 23 hours before its batch is encoded, as Aptabase drops an event more than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a day old while answering 200, the hour to spare for a queue on the server and clocks that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disagree;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one too large for a request of 1,000,000 bytes on its own.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Characters are counted in UTF-16, as .NET counts them, so an emoji counts two. The destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports each record left out as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property of the plan whose name would be left out."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A request is encoded once and retried as it is, so each request’s deadline is 23 hours after its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest record was tracked: one still failing by then, a slow upload’s 418 included, isn’t sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again, which Aptabase would answer with 200 while storing nothing. It is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"text":". A clock that reads NaN or infinite has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every record reported. An event from the future, by a clock that runs ahead, is sent, and Aptabase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores it at the time it arrives.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The 23 hours are measured by the device’s own clock, but Aptabase measures a day by its server’s.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"On a device whose clock runs about a day behind, a record tracked just now carries a timestamp a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"day old: the encoder sends it, and Aptabase drops it while answering 200, so the record is lost","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without a report.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What Aptabase doesn’t report","anchor":"What-Aptabase-doesnt-report","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase answers 200 to a request with a key of no app, of a deleted app, or of an account it has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"locked, such as one past its plan’s monthly events, and stores nothing: check that the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events reach the app’s Live View after setting the destination up. It doesn’t remove duplicates,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a record sent again, after a retry whose answer was lost or a store’s redelivery, is counted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"twice.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase takes 20 requests a second from one IP address, and answers 429 past it, which the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination retries on its backoff."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Aptabase receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to Aptabase, in its cloud or on your own server, through its events API."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Aptabase","title":"Sending to Aptabase","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing Destinations"}]},"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AptabaseBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"title":"aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Aptabase app of ","type":"text"},{"code":"appKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", at the region its key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names or, for a self-hosted key, at ","type":"text"},{"code":"host","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", marking every event as a debug event or not as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" says, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"aptabase","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"appKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text"